<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Gallen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Gallen is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, capital of the canton of St. Gallen, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>. It grew around the Abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a>, founded in the 8th century, and became a free imperial city whose linen trade made it wealthy and often set it against the abbots. The abbey precinct, with its baroque cathedral and famous library, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-gallen.jpg" alt="St. Gallen" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: albinfo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St.Gallen_vonDreiweieren_09.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
